SEC 6  THE PIN'S FOUR FALSIFIERS, each with its verdict
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  F1  'A_D is not odd under the order-dual * at the fixture.'
      VERDICT: DOES NOT FIRE AS WRITTEN, FIRES IN ITS SPIRIT.
      As written: A_D IS odd under * on the common carrier — but
      only as 0 = -0 (T1.7), because A_D == 0 identically (T1.1).
      In its spirit: the two reversals are the same map ONLY on
      2-event histories (T1.4) and are different maps everywhere
      else (T1.5); and * is not even an operation on v10's records
      (T1.9: 1264 of 1558 records have no in-family dual).
      => Clause 3's bridge is NOT established.  The corpus does
         not gain two unrelated reversal-odd channels; it gains
         one channel with no content and one operation with no
         domain.

  F2  'The sqrt(q) round-trip transport is identically 1 on every
      delete-then-insert cycle of the generated line.'
      VERDICT: FIRED — AT CLOSED SCOPE, ON GRAMMAR 1, FOR THE RAW WEIGHT.
      758 independent cycles at grammar 1 depth<=5 and 63971 closed
      exchange squares over every base (depth <= 7), all exactly 1;
      every up-edge single-valued.  The round supplies the reason: it
      is a THEOREM for this grammar (T5.L1/L3/L4/L5/L6), and the
      T2 half of it is forced by T1.8 alone (T2.0).
      THREE SCOPE CLAUSES, all measured here, all narrowing it:
        (i)  GRAMMAR.  At transport scope (d42b1) A_D is NOT zero: 100 of
             3100 closed squares are non-unit (spectrum {'1/2': 82, '2/3': 2, '3/2': 6, '2': 10}),
             plus 40 half-open squares (A_D = +/- infinity).  T6.1/T6.2.
        (ii) INSTRUMENT.  The record-deletion-graph census cannot see them:
             0 of 100 defective squares close at record level.  T6.3.
        (iii) WEIGHT.  For the process's own conditional kernel q/M the same
             grammar-1 record graph has non-trivial holonomy, <5/4> in R+.  T4.3.
      => THE GENERATED LINE IS FLAT AT CLOSED SCOPE, IN GRAMMAR 1, FOR THE RAW
         BUDGET WEIGHT — and that is exactly the object D42b4's prod sqrt(q)
         lift transports, so D71 Clause 3's '+1' is forced FOR THAT LIFT.
         It is not a statement about the generated line as such.

  F3  'L_dual's dual-conjugation error on the generated line's
      channels is non-zero.'
      VERDICT: DOES NOT FIRE (computed: worst L_dual error over every cell = 0.000e+00)
      — and the reason is worse than a
      failure would have been.  The error is 0 on v10's
      channels, at k = 2, 3, 4 AND 5, on both domains and both orbit
      readings.  But T3.CTRL shows the 0 is an ALGEBRAIC IDENTITY
      of the ansatz: adversarial (E,O) integers from nowhere score
      0 too.  Reproducing it is evidence only that the port made E
      even and O odd, which it did by construction.  A2c shows the
      same of v7's own control number: 1.8210207... is exactly
      2*exp(-3/32), the closed form at E = 3 — a constant of the
      ansatz, not a measurement of the N=9 universe.
      Scope, both readings run: on the odd-orbit reading the even
      channel is identically 0 on the v10-closed domain (T3.C), so
      even the naive control scores 0 and there is nothing to
      discriminate; on the all-orbits reading the discrimination
      does reappear (T3.D).  => the surviving v7 form TRANSFERS,
      FORMALLY, and the transfer is empty of substrate content.

  F4  'The round-trip defect exists but is not U(1)-valued.'
      VERDICT: FIRES — and the first delivery's 'not reached,
      vacuously' was WRONG (round MAJOR 1 + MAJOR 2).  A defect exists,
      on two independent objects, and it is R+-valued with no argument:
        (a) normalised connection, grammar 1: True — image group
            <5/4> subset R+ on the same 758-cycle record graph (T4.3), which
            is D65's committed mass-ratio coboundary (QUOTES['d65']).
        (b) raw transport scope, grammar 2: True — 100 closed squares
            with ratios in ['1/2', '2', '2/3', '3/2'] plus 40 half-open
            squares at A_D = +/- infinity (T6.1, T6.2).
      => The founding slogan is refuted IN F4's OWN DIRECTION, not one step
